## Key Design Decisions

### Chat Selector Mobile

**Layout:** Full-screen flat list with thin divider lines between rows. Each row shows title, date line ("edited 3d ago · created 02/20/25"), and the active global view's content (summary, notes, highlights, or branches).

**Bottom tab bar:** Four icon+label tabs (Summary, Notes, Highlights, Branches) with a sliding blue indicator line. Tap to switch views. No swipe-to-switch — swipe is reserved for selection mode.

**Swipe-right → selection mode:** Swiping right anywhere on the list (>60px horizontal, <400ms, 1.8x more horizontal than vertical) enters selection mode globally. All rows get animated checkboxes sliding in from the left. Tapping a row toggles its checkbox.

**Floating bulk action bar:** Overlays the top of the list area when in selection mode. Shows selected count, total size, pin/regenerate/trash icon buttons, and an X to exit. Subtle shadow, rounded corners. An animated spacer pushes the first list item down so it's not hidden behind the bar.

**Top bar:** Settings and Star (with amber count badge) on the left. "+ Chat" button on the right.

**Favorites:** Bottom sheet with drag handle, slides up from bottom with backdrop. Cards are touch-sized with copy and remove buttons.

**View content rendering:** Summary clamps to 2 lines. Notes and highlights show up to 2 items with "+N more" overflow. Branches show parent/child relationships with family color bars. Rows with no content for the active view de-emphasize to 40% opacity.

### Settings Mobile

**Navigation pattern:** Accordion — all 7 sections listed as expandable items. Only one open at a time. Tapping a new section closes the current one.

**Sections preserved (all 7):** API Configuration, Model Preferences, Usage & Spending, Context & Defaults, Data & Backups, Appearance, About & Security.

**Top bar:** Back arrow + "Settings" title with bottom border divider.

**Accordion headers:** Icon in a rounded square (tinted blue when open), section label + subtitle, rotating chevron. Content animates in with height + opacity via SPRING_SMOOTH.

**Touch adaptations:** Inputs use rounded-xl and py-3 for larger touch targets. Validate button is full-width below key input. Radio options have py-3.5 padding and 20px radio circles. Segmented controls replace desktop pill toggles with flex-1 items. All buttons use active: states instead of hover:.

**Modals → bottom sheets:** Export, Import, and Delete Confirmation all use a reusable BottomSheet component with drag handle + header pattern. Max height 85vh.

**Shared components:** SettingsCard, ToggleSwitch (larger 44px wide), RadioOption, SegmentedControl, InfoBanner, BottomSheet — all designed for touch-first use.

### Conversation UI (Swift Mode)

#### Top Bar — Minimal

**Single centered grip icon** (`GripHorizontal`) opens the unified panel. No left/right sidebar icons, no plus button, no borders. The grip icon is color-coded by context health (green/amber/red), serving as an ambient signal that also draws the eye enough for discoverability.

#### Message Cards — Tap to Select

**No three-dot menu, no header divider, no message numbers.** Cards are clean content containers with a `#DDDDE3` border and `rounded-2xl` corners.

**Persistent indicators:** Dusty gold star and note icon appear in the top-left corner when a message is favorited or has a note attached. These are small (12px) and subtle.

**Tap to select:** Tapping a card animates its border to blue (`#4A7AE5`). The card expands at the bottom to reveal an inline action row with 7 icon+label buttons: Favorite (dusty gold), Branch (purple), Note (amber), Copy (grey), Move (blue), Hide (grey), Delete (red). Tapping outside or tapping the card again deselects and collapses.

**Ghost text state:** Dashed border, 55% opacity, with a "Continue" button below the card matching production behavior.

**User messages offset right (ml-8), assistant messages offset left (mr-8).** Branch indicators show on the left edge with a purple GitBranch icon and connecting line.

#### Gesture Vocabulary

| Gesture | Action | Feedback |
|---------|--------|----------|
| Swipe left | New blank chat | Blue toast: "New chat started" (1.5s) |
| Swipe right | Instant compressed branch from last message | Purple toast: "Branching with compressed summary" + subtitle (2s) |
| Tap card | Select → expand inline action row | Blue border animation, action row slides in |
| Tap grip icon | Open unified panel | Bottom sheet slides up |

**Swipe detection:** >80px horizontal displacement, horizontal-dominant (2x ratio to vertical), completed within 400ms.

**Swipe right branching** defaults to compressed summary mode — no panel, no choice dialog. For Full History or branching from a specific message, users use the card's expanded action row (tap card → Branch icon).

#### Unified Panel (Bottom Sheet)

Replaces both the left and right desktop sidebars with a single bottom sheet. Organized as a scrollable list of expandable sections:

| Row | Icon | Expandable | Contents |
|-----|------|------------|----------|
| Chats | MessageSquare (blue) | No | Navigates back to chat selector |
| Contents | List (grey) | Yes | TOC derived from user messages (truncated to 55 chars), tap scrolls to message |
| Highlights | Highlighter (green) | Yes | Highlight items with tap-to-cycle navigation and long-press-to-delete |
| Branches | GitBranch (purple) | Yes | Branch list with active state highlighting |
| Collaboration Mode | Settings2 (blue) | Yes | 5 preset toggles with radio-style selection |
| Review | BookOpen (grey) | No | Opens review |
| Export to Markdown | FileText (grey) | No | Triggers export |
| Compress Context | Activity (amber) | No | Opens branch panel |

**Only one section expanded at a time.** Chevron rotates 180° when open. Badge counts shown for Highlights and Branches.

**Highlight interaction:** Tap a highlight item to cycle through occurrences in the conversation (scrolls to each one). Counter shows "2/4" position. Long-press (600ms) to delete with fade-out animation. Hint text: "Tap to jump between occurrences. Hold to remove."

**Collaboration Mode presets:** Challenge Artifacts, Show Reasoning, Push Back on Me, Offer Alternatives, Flag Uncertainty. Each is a toggle with a filled radio circle and description text.

**No keyboard shortcuts section** (mobile doesn't need it). **No context health section** (context health is communicated through the grip icon and send button colors).

#### Send Button — Context Health Indicator

The send button doubles as an ambient context health signal. It's a `rounded-xl` (rounded square) with a thin border.

| State | Border | Fill | Arrow |
|-------|--------|------|-------|
| Empty, low context | #DDDDE3 | transparent | green |
| Empty, medium context | #DDDDE3 | transparent | amber |
| Empty, high context | #DDDDE3 | transparent | red |
| Text entered, low context | green | green | white |
| Text entered, medium context | amber | amber | white |
| Text entered, high context | red | red | white |
| Streaming | red | red | white (Square/stop icon) |

This eliminates the need for a dedicated context health panel — users get continuous passive awareness through two color-coded controls (grip icon + send button) that bookend the screen.

#### Input Area

**Always-visible border** (`#DDDDE3` default, `#4A7AE5` on focus) on white background. Auto-expanding textarea (up to 120px). Placeholder: "Type here, or swipe left to start a new chat."

**No divider line** above the input area — it sits cleanly below the messages.

#### Design Token: Dusty Gold

Production uses `#C4A94D` (Dusty Gold) for favorites throughout — not the generic amber `#E5A620`. This is used for the star icon fill/stroke, favorite card borders on hover (desktop), and the Favorite action icon in the expanded card row.

